### Processor usage with queue name and worker options

Source: https://github.com/nestjs/bull/blob/master/_autodocs/api-reference/bullmq-decorators.md

Marks a class extending WorkerHost as a queue worker for the 'audio' queue with concurrency 5. The process method receives a Job and returns a promise.

```typescript
import { Processor, WorkerHost } from '@nestjs/bullmq';
import { Job } from 'bullmq';

@Processor('audio', { concurrency: 5 })
export class AudioConsumer extends WorkerHost {
  async process(job: Job<{ file: string }>): Promise<any> {
    return transcode(job.data.file);
  }
}
```

